    {
      "caption": "Stationary is not always max or min",
      "duration_ms": 7000,
      "id": "s5",
      "narration": "The classic slip: seeing dy over dx equal zero and calling it a maximum or minimum without checking. Y equals x cubed at x equals zero is stationary — and still climbing.",
